  "quality_formula": "quality(pair) = ( sum over sub-dims d with weight w_d > 0 of w_d * (app_scores[a][d] + app_scores[b][d]) / 2 ) / ( sum of w_d ). This is the AVERAGE of the two platforms on each property (not best-of-pair). If no sub-dimension has weight > 0, quality = 0.",
  "raw_axis_values": "coverage = pair coverage in the chosen denominator; complementarity = net-new percent in the chosen denominator; quality = quality(pair) above; cost = total_cost; class_balance = class_balance; sample_volume = joint_volume_uL; ms_fit = 1 if the pair contains a mass-spectrometry platform (Seer Proteograph XT or Biognosys TrueDiscovery) else 0.",
  "pair_coverage_rule": "EXACT for all four numeric denominators as of v2.9 (P13: the independence-model estimate has been removed). drug_targets and fda_biomarkers are exact set intersections against their external reference lists (1,450 ChEMBL drug targets; 217 FDA-approved biomarkers, Bhowmick et al. 2021). proteome_canonical and proteome_atlas_union are exact unions of each platform's own accession-level list, computed directly from public/proteins.json.",
  "normalisation": "Per axis, min-max across the fifteen pairs to [0,1]: n = (x - min)/(max - min); for inverted axes (cost, sample_volume) n = (max - x)/(max - min). If max == min the range is treated as 1 so the axis contributes 0.",
  "composite_formula": "composite(pair) = ( sum over axes of weight[axis] * n[axis] ) / ( sum over axes of weight[axis] ). Winner of a scenario = the pair with the highest composite (discovery mode, all fifteen pairs eligible).",
