  },
  "pathway_coverage_disclosure": "The UI's optional Reactome pathway selector shows each pair's precomputed pathway coverage (source: reactome_pathways.json, pathway_coverage.json) as a descriptive figure alongside composite, with a view-only toggle to re-order the ranked list by it. It is not an eighth axis (not in the seven-entry axes array above), not a twelfth priority (not in priority_to_lever above), and not a fifth coverage denominator (not in denominators above): it enters no formula in this spec and does not affect composite, so it is outside the priority_sweep's input space and requires no change to any scored quantity here.",
  "priority_sweep": "All combinations of 1, 2, or 3 of the eleven priorities (11 + 55 + 165 = 231), evaluated over the four numeric denominators = 924 scenarios. Fully deterministic; no RNG.",
  "bootstrap_ci": "Per pair, 2,000-resample bootstrap over the drug-target universe (n=1,450): draws ~ Binomial(1450, coverage_pct/100) / 1450 via numpy.random.default_rng(seed=42), 2.5th/97.5th percentiles. Computed once per pair, in pair order, immediately after the platform/pair data is loaded and before the sweeps run (order affects the RNG stream and must match for exact reproduction).",
